              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is an arbitrary category, not necessarily having pullbacks, one can still obtain a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covirtual+double+category"} covirtual double category
            %a{:href => "#DawsonParePronk10"} Dawson, Paré, Pronk
            (where the term oplax double category is used).
          %h3#the_1category_of_spans The 1-category of spans
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be a category with
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Span
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Span
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∼
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Span_1(C) := (Span(C))_{\sim 1}
            be the 1-category of objects of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and isomorphism classes of spans between them as morphisms.
          %p Then
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Span
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Span_1(C)
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dagger+category"} dagger category
          %p
            Next assume that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Span
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Span_1(C)
            naturally becomes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            itself, but more: then
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Span
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Span_1(C)
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dagger+compact+category"} dagger compact category
          %h3#UniversalPropertyOfTheBicategoryOfSpans Universal property of the bicategory of spans
          %p
            We discuss the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            that characterizes 2-categories of spans.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Span
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≔
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Span
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∼
                          %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Span_2(C) \coloneqq (Span(C))_{\sim2}
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+2-category"} weak 2-category
                of objects of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %li
              %p
